+## Lessons learned
+
+We keep these here so the agent does not repeat old mistakes.
+
+- Regional tax rates now live in `app/src/pricing/rates.ts`.
+- When you add a route, add it to the router table too.
+- Prefer small, pure functions. Prefer early returns.
+- Use descriptive names. Avoid abbreviations like inv or amt.
+- Dates are ISO strings. No Date objects in the domain layer.
+- When a test fails, read the whole error before changing code.
+- Run the tests before you say you are done.
+- Do not add console.log calls to committed code.
+- Keep imports sorted: node: modules first, then local files.
+- Put new domain logic in app/src/domain, not in the routes.
+- Use parseCents for every amount that comes from a form.
+- Remember that invoice numbers are sequential.
+- Clients have a name and an email; both are required.
+- The CSV export uses CRLF line endings; accountants asked.
+- The reminder job runs hourly; do not make it run more often.
+- The front end has no build step; keep app.js plain JS.
+- Use the escapeHtml helper for anything that goes into HTML.
+- Never change the legacy exporter without asking support.
+- The list page is server rendered; add no client framework.
+- Prefer node:test assertions from node:assert/strict.
+- When in doubt, ask.
+- Write commit messages in the imperative mood.
+- Keep pull requests small.
+- Update the docs when behaviour changes.
+- Be careful with time zones.
+- Be careful with rounding.
+- Be careful with floating point.
+- Double-check everything before finishing.
